{
  "_comment": [
    "Copy the 'creo-jlink' entry below into your AI client's own mcp.json.",
    "",
    "There is nothing about Creo, hosts or ports here on purpose: discovery is just a command and",
    "its arguments. Everything installation-specific lives in paths.yaml, which the server finds on",
    "its own (see Config/paths.example.yaml for the search order).",
    "",
    "The server bootstraps itself: on startup it reads paths.yaml and, if PTCNMSPORT and",
    "PRO_COMM_MSG_EXE are not already set, re-executes once with the correct environment and with",
    "pfcasync.jar on the classpath. That is why 'java -jar mcp.jar' alone is enough.",
    "",
    "If paths.yaml is not in one of the default locations, add it explicitly:",
    "  \"args\": [\"-Dasyncjlink.config=C:\\\\Tools\\\\AsyncJLink\\\\paths.yaml\", \"-jar\", \"C:\\\\Tools\\\\AsyncJLink\\\\mcp.jar\"]",
    "",
    "This server publishes every J-Link operation as its own tool. If your client struggles with a",
    "tool list that size, cap the page size and it will paginate:",
    "  \"args\": [\"-Dasyncjlink.mcp.pageSize=100\", \"-jar\", \"C:\\\\Tools\\\\AsyncJLink\\\\mcp.jar\"]"
  ],

  "mcpServers": {
    "creo-jlink": {
      "command": "java",
      "args": ["-jar", "C:\\Tools\\AsyncJLink\\mcp.jar"]
    }
  }
}
